WEBVTT

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.310
<i>Haruko once told me that</i>

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.700
<i>all Japanese people have an 
abnormal love for these flowers.</i>

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.570
Yikes!

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.860
Ren, did you sleep with the window open?

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.370
I'll clean it when I get back.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:32.230
It's fine. I'll do it while you're at school.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.640
Morning, Ren.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.720
Anyway, do you like them?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.540
The cherry blossoms?

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.410
Yeah.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.180
Your room has the best view.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.180
I really wanted to show them to you.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.440
I'm glad we moved in time.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.290
Pretty, right?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.170
Yeah.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.650
Breakfast is ready, and your lunch, too.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.840
After you eat, I'll give you a ride.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.200
I can take the train.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.290
Didn't you freeze up at the 
ticket gate the other day?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Sometimes he's really more 
considerate than he needs to be.</i>

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.610
Good morning, Ren.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.510
Oh?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.020
Souryou still uses a traditional uniform?

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.310
That's pretty unusual these days.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.020
Really?

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.020
Even though we're twins, 
I started getting taller than Aki

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.400
right around your age.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.760
You're not supposed to talk about that!

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.900
Ren looks so stoic in his uniform.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.810
It's kind of a turn-on...

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.030
Shut up, pervert.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.040
Anyway, Bro...

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.790
You said you wanted to open a store, 
but what kind of store?

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.270
Iku and I have been talking about opening a café.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.830
We'll close at 6:00 PM and...

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.490
6:00 PM? Do you even want to run a café?!

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:21.290
I won't be able to cook dinner 
if we're open too late.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.800
It'll turn into a bar at night, 
but someone else will be handling that.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.450
And Ikuyoshi's family grows organic vegetables.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:34.710
I even have an ex-host friend who 
went back home to be a fisherman.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.270
The spiny lobsters we ate 
at New Year's came from him.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.280
Those were good.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.200
Right? And one of my former 
customers is an interior designer.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.200
I'm lucky to have so much help.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.330
<i>Come to think of it, this guy...</i>

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.790
<i>...has always had...</i>

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.330
<i>...a crowd of people surrounding him.</i>

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.810
Ren, what's wrong? Get in.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.340
<i>I more or less understand 
what kind of man Haru is.</i>

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.640
Where did you get this car?

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:11.350
Um... It was given to be as a goodbye 
present when I quit the club.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.330
No, wait! I tried to refuse it,

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.860
but since I was quitting, I just couldn't say no...

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.910
That's enough.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.180
I know, I know. I'm sorry.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.210
But...

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.620
<i>I know it's not worth getting 
mad at everything he says.</i>

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.870
<i>I know it's not, but I still get angry!</i>

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.380
Since I'm your guardian, 
let me take a look around your school.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.380
You look more like a suspicious intruder.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.840
If anyone asks, you'd better 
call me your brother.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.890
All right, I'm going to punish you, then.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.110
Starting today, you have to kiss me 
when you leave and come home.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.510
That's stupid.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:00.900
If you refuse, starting today, rice will 
disappear from our family meals for a while.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.530
<i>I'm going to kill him!</i>

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.160
Do you hate kissing me that much?

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.280
If you don't like it, I won't do it anymore.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.500
I've never not liked it.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.290
Really?

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:20.730
Haru.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.000
I'm going now.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.380
All right. Good boy.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.300
Call me once you get out of class.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.930
I'll come pick you up.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.280
<i>I feel like I've lost in all kinds of ways...</i>

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.340
Kaidou.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.820
Kaidou!

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.030
Kaidou Ren!

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.360
Who are you?

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.650
I've been sitting behind you for three days, 
and you're asking who I am?

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.660
I'm Kurosaki. Kurosaki Juuzen!

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:00.380
I called your name a bunch of times. 
Are you deaf or something?

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.150
Oh... Just call me Ren.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.840
I'm not used to that surname yet.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:06.670
Okay...

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.240
Your parents are remarried, too?

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.800
No, not quite...

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.310
Well, whatever.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.580
I became a Kurosaki this year.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.180
I can't get used to the name or Tokyo.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.190
Anyway...

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.070
Was that foreign dude this 
morning your boyfriend?

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.070
Haru's Japanese.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.480
His name's Haru, huh?

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.390
What about it?

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:35.700
Oh, I just thought you must be close, 
to be kissing in front of the shoe lockers.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.040
We don't normally do that outside.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.220
Where do you normally do it?

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:44.380
At home. He's always been 
particular about that stuff.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.290
You live together?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.080
Yeah.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.910
<i>He looks totally clueless, 
but he's living with a man?</i>

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.470
<i>Tokyo dudes are way more 
advanced than I thought!</i>

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.500
Never mind.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.610
I'm glad you guys love each other so much.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:00.480
Love?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.600
I mean that your feelings are mutual.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.420
Maybe...

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.730
I don't know if it's mutual.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:13.120
Right now, Haru's "love" and my "love" 
are two totally different things.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.200
Ren, are you leaving already?

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:26.290
Didn't our homeroom teacher 
just tell you to join a club?

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.630
It's not mandatory.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.570
The teacher just pointed out that I don't 
communicate with others enough.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:32.260
Huh?

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.310
Our homeroom teacher called me an old fart.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.970
Well, you are.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:41.010
The way you talk is so formal.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:43.850
You're like a modern-day samurai.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.220
Well, my Japanese isn't as strange as yours!

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.280
I'm just speaking in the Kansai dialect!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.030
Oh, it's an accent?

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.580
You've just made an enemy out of 
every Kansai-born person in Japan!

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.340
What?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.840
I told you to call once class was over.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.190
How do you know I'm about to leave?

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:09.120
Well, all I had to do was look.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.420
Hey! Can you see me?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.180
Welcome home, Ren.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.310
Hey...

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.690
We're not at home yet.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.190
That's too bad.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.560
You shouldn't have come.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:27.130
You stand out too much.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.540
What's your problem? I came to pick you up.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.190
I'm not a child.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:35.160
I know. I just want to spend time with you.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.180
<i>Oh, boy.</i>

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.710
<i>If that's what he's dealing with, 
the odds are against him for sure.</i>

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:42.090
<i>The girls aren't likely to leave him alone.</i>

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.540
Ren!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.440
What?

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.040
Let me borrow your phone.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.090
Thanks.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.050
There.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:54.550
Here. Do you remember my name?

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.520
Kurosaki Juuzen.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.490
I remember because it's a weird name.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.590
Wha...

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.280
Don't call it weird!

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.180
Well, whatever.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.130
I live in the dorm here.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.690
If you ever need anything, call me.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.090
Is he your friend?

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.920
Kurosaki Juuzen. He's in my class.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:18.420
He talks and acts a little weird, 
but he's not a bad guy.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.610
That's high praise coming from you.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.910
I'll try to remember him, too.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.170
La-la... Haru-san, are you home?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.170
The interior decor plans and samples are—

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:38.340
What, Iku? Did you see a cockroach?

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.300
Ren.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.450
Brother, welcome home.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.060
Ikuyoshi, keep it down.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:44.870
I'm going to change.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.810
You don't have to do that.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.780
Ren Ren and Haru-san, the way you flirt 
with each other is bad for my heart.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:52.760
Give me a break.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.280
Huh? What do you mean?

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.350
He asked me what I meant!

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.120
Just kissing someone hello is normal.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.230
We're brothers.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.720
Maybe it is normal.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.960
You know how our brother is.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.110
Normal?

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:08.510
Yeah. After all, these guys...

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.580
They're basically foreigners.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.090
Right...

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.070
<i>It's all been cleaned up...</i>

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.150
<i>I really wanted to show them to you.</i>

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.280
<i>Pretty, right?</i>

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:33.770
How long are these flowers 
going to keep blooming?

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:42.420
Ren?

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:43.950
Haru?

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.590
I'm going to check out Iku's family's farm.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:52.660
I can't take you to school. 
Will you be okay by yourself?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.280
I'll be fine.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.800
Okay. I hope you make it 
through the ticket gate okay.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:04.950
Here I go!

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:13.160
You again?

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.280
Are you okay? This time, 
calm down and take it slow.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.700
Sorry for bothering you 
so early in the morning.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.450
See you later.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.900
Be careful.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.350
Thanks for coming.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.710
I love your parents. They're so generous!

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.850
What should I make for dinner tonight?

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.090
You're eating with us, right?

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.340
Of course.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.710
Wait, Haru-san, have you 
always liked cooking so much?

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:43.140
I mostly stopped cooking once 
I started living on my own,

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.350
but now that I'm living with Ren...

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.920
Well, he is a growing boy, huh?

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.890
Actually, Ren Ren is pretty small for his age.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:56.360
He's sensitive about that. 
Don't mention it in front of him.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.360
Got it.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:03.110
Haru-san?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.610
Oh, well...

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:09.620
He's gotten sick twice since 
he came to Japan last year.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.870
It was just a cold,

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.710
but when he lived in Canada, 
he never got sick.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.960
When I was a host, I didn't have any time,

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.770
so I always bought him 
convenience store lunches to eat.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:24.230
But Ren never complained,

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.300
and no matter how late I came 
home, he'd always get up.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.350
I just...

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:34.450
So that's why you're running a restaurant 
right next to your house this time.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:35.880
Yeah.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.580
Hey, Iku...

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:42.360
If he doesn't grow any taller, 
do you think it'll be my fault?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.740
Haru-san, watch the road! The road!

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.000
Aki? Shima?

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.520
Work (won't need dinner)

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.500
Haru -> Chiba (will return before dinner)

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.500
Aki -> Class

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.500
Shima -> Class

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.500
No work

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.500
Hello?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.930
Took you long enough!

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.580
I just got home.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.380
Oh, it's you, Ren.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:03.630
The landlord?

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:09.850
I mean... I understand that Ren Ren 
is a very dear brother to you, but...

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.230
Not just a brother.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.630
He's my darling honey.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:18.170
I don't even know where to start on that one!

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.620
And how serious are you?

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.870
Isn't Ren cute?

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.720
I'll kill you if you touch him, though.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.080
You say that now,

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.630
but what are you going to do 
if he brings home a girl one day?

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.980
It'll be fine.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:34.000
I'm pretty confident that I could 
beat the girls around here.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.800
Haru-san, don't tell me you and Ren Ren...

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.200
You must be joking.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.880
I'd never go for a kid with so little sex appeal.

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:52.640
Sorry I'm just a kid with no sex appeal!

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.430
Huh? Brother, welcome home.

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.650
Didn't Ren just go out to meet you?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.400
Did you hear that he's going to 
take care of Onodera's raccoon dog?

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:10.130
Until his leg heals completely, 
he's going to stay with his grandson.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.660
Brother, are you listening?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.660
Jump

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:17.040
It's your fault, Iku.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:18.260
Huh?!

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.560
Why me?

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.630
This is a disaster!

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.780
What is this?

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.010
You put a lot of effort into tonight's dinner.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.140
And it's all Ren's favorites.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.220
Your brother

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.270
wore the expression of a man carrying 
his cross while he was cooking dinner.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.560
Oh... Well...

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.390
It's good for him to realize 
every once in a while

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.530
just how loved he is.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:49.680
Ren? Dinner's ready.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:53.260
I made all your favorites tonight.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.970
I even got strawberries.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.040
Silence

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:01.210
If you don't come out soon, 
Iku will eat everything.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.470
Go ahead and eat!

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:11.150
Do you like those flowers, too?

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.130
You're so gloomy.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.400
Is Ren Ren still mad?

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.720
He hasn't spoken to me in five days...

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.730
What am I supposed to do?

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:39.190
Work. Here are the plans for the café.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:41.460
Maybe I'll go walk the dog...

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.920
Why are you trying to escape from reality?

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.770
You're eating in the cafeteria again? 
You always brought lunch before.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.190
How many days has it been?

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.430
I can do what I want.

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:58.040
Well, that's true.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:02.650
But it sucks that the cafeteria 
here is kinda expensive.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:03.840
Is it?

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.440
Are you a rich kid, too?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.370
I don't think so...

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.900
I'm just not in the habit of using cash.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.050
That's what you call a rich kid.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:18.120
Until my mom got remarried 
and we moved to Tokyo,

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.190
all I thought about was money.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.170
I know I'm fortunate.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.830
Really? That's good.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.600
A lot of people don't realize it.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.920
But Ren, you're lonely, aren't you?

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.780
I was lonely.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:39.140
My mom didn't say a word to me

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.460
when my dad disappeared 
and left behind his debts,

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.600
or when she decided to get remarried.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:48.110
Everything worked out in the end, though.

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:52.170
And to top it off, they're having a kid next year.

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:55.120
What would it be like to have 
a sibling 16 years younger?

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:58.550
It means you'll have someone

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:01.840
who'll hold your hand without any misgiving.

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:03.810
You won't be lonely.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.960
You think so?

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:07.190
Earlier, you said that

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:10.590
some people don't realize 
how fortunate they are.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.690
Ren, do you like fried chicken? 
You can have mine!

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:19.610
Eat lots so you'll grow big.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.850
What are you doing?

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.100
Don't touch my sacred salmon lunch!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.680
What the heck? If you're a man, 
you've gotta eat meat!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.550
I don't want it! I want my salmon!

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:28.930
I'll feed it to you!

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:34.290
There's just leaves now.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.350
Oh, you mean the cherry trees?

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:39.330
They're only in bloom for a short time.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:42.330
These are some impressive strawberries.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.120
Aren't they? I heard they're Ren Ren's favorite.

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.620
What, Ren?

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.670
If you're not going to eat them, I will.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.320
Aki! I never said—

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:59.860
Iku, did we get an estimate 
for the interior decor?

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:00.850
Yeah.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:05.410
<i>I always realize, after the fact, 
just how much he loves me.</i>

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:14.650
Wh-What?

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:17.740
Haru, it's me.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.130
Ren, if you want to sneak into my bed,

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.000
could you let me know beforehand from now on?

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.750
Sneak into your bed?

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.220
Yeah.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:35.140
It means sneaking into someone's 
bedroom for a nighttime visit.

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.840
Just like you're doing right now.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:38.110
Haru...

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:42.390
All the cherry blossoms have fallen.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.420
Yeah. They're in their leaf stage now.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.270
You'll have to wait until next year.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:51.770
Then how long do I have to keep 
sleeping in that room alone?

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.860
<i>Is it because of what I said?</i>

00:18:58.860 --> 00:18:59.780
Haru?

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.410
Haru?

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:04.760
Have you been wanting to come 
to this room this whole time?

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.450
Yeah.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.230
And you were holding back?

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:07.970
Yeah.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.230
I see...

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:13.390
I guess we've been sleeping in the same 
room since we started living together.

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:16.010
I know I'm just a kid with zero sex appeal.

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:17.050
So sue me.

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.470
No, I'm sorry, Ren.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.610
I'm glad you came.

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:25.560
I don't think I could've taken it anymore.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.570
Liar.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.050
I'm not lying.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:32.310
Some things are hard to touch because 
they're so important to you, Ren.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:35.470
Like those strawberries?

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.710
Strawberries?

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.820
Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.690
It's a waste to eat them all at once.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.780
I see. But I...

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.790
Ow!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.190
...can't stand to see them eaten by someone else!

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:51.290
From now on, I'll eat them all at once!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.460
What the heck are you talking about?

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.800
<i>Japanese strawberries cultivated 
in a greenhouse are fantastic.</i>

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:05.620
<i>But I've never tasted anything more delicious</i>

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:10.440
<i>than the blackberries Ren once picked for me.</i>

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:14.380
Good morning.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.160
Huh? Where's Haru-san?

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.630
Still asleep.

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.580
Ren hasn't gotten up yet, either.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.140
Well, it's Sunday.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.700
We can let them sleep in.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.510
Seriously? But I skipped breakfast!

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:29.900
That's why you've been coming over so much?

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.590
Well, Haru-san's cooking is just <i>too</i> good.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:34.290
Don't stress it like that!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.210
Looks like he's up.

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:39.550
Morning...

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:45.100
Th-The room next door is 
Haru-san's bedroom, right?

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.100
Yeah.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.430
Bro, I'm hungry.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:51.600
Give me a minute.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.590
Ren, do you want milk?

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:54.310
Yeah.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:01.820
Why do you have a bite mark on your neck?

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.620
Did the raccoon dog bite you?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.820
What? This is your fault, you know!

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:07.320
Huh?

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:12.410
I got bitten because you 
stole Ren's strawberries!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.350
Do you have any idea what he means?

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:17.520
I think he meant exactly what he said.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:21.210
Ren, you two made up?

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.170
We weren't fighting to begin with.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.180
So stubborn...

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:30.230
And he's not even house-trained.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.930
He went in my bed this morning.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.070
Really?

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:37.460
Come to think of it, can you 
house-train a raccoon dog?

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.810
Um...

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:43.570
That animal Ren Ren is carrying 
isn't a raccoon dog, right?

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.380
Isn't it a dog?

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:47.370
Huh?

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:55.230
<i>The relationship between the eldest and 
youngest brothers remains as delicate as ever,</i>

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.430
<i>but they're taking things one step at a time.</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Next Time
